{"schema_version":3,"catalogue_version":1,"id":"bco:10-3","provision":"BCO 10-3","book":"bco","book_name":"Book of Church Order","abbreviation":"BCO","reference":"10-3","title":"Section 10-3","supplementary":false,"canonical_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/provisions/bco/10-3/","reader_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-constitution-reader/#bco/10-3","current_text":{"html":"<p>The pastor is, for prudential reasons, moderator of the Session. The moderator of the Presbytery may be elected at each stated meeting of the court, or for a period of time up to one year. The moderator of the General Assembly shall be chosen at each stated meeting; he, or in case of his absence the last moderator present or the oldest minister longest a member of the court, shall open the next meeting with a sermon unless it is impracticable, and shall hold the chair until a new moderator be chosen. The moderator has all authority necessary for the preservation of order and for the proper and expeditious conduct of all business before the court, and for convening and adjourning the court according to its own ruling. In any emergency, he may by circular letter change the time or place, or both, of meeting to which the court stands adjourned, giving reasonable notice thereof.</p>","text":"The pastor is, for prudential reasons, moderator of the Session. The moderator of the Presbytery may be elected at each stated meeting of the court, or for a period of time up to one year. The moderator of the General Assembly shall be chosen at each stated meeting; he, or in case of his absence the last moderator present or the oldest minister longest a member of the court, shall open the next meeting with a sermon unless it is impracticable, and shall hold the chair until a new moderator be chosen. The moderator has all authority necessary for the preservation of order and for the proper and expeditious conduct of all business before the court, and for convening and adjourning the court according to its own ruling. In any emergency, he may by circular letter change the time or place, or both, of meeting to which the court stands adjourned, giving reasonable notice thereof."},"source":{"name":"PCA Constitution Reader","revision":"3215b08b64db0d1ab36e0721b999ec192d812d74","edition":"Current Reader text","files":{"bco.js":"c88e552545b73fd9690de620b237895b7ea52a94bed8e95690c116bf76be8ae5","wcf.js":"1ebf9e54223f7fe4e728a3e640c833a435af825d74b5ef3d4b04687685538a0d","wlc.js":"f6977e761ea4ccc93b07fcacfd0391890cb05b42f4317d807fa293c078d9b051","wsc.js":"dd775417f7ef21e3283bacad5e6ef193c41d64d03bd5a2e8fb934ccca8cb8e53","rao.js":"49808bbb0e95abdc3b07506c87dde0d62d087851e869b49c0f1f2424986450ec"}},"input_fingerprint":"e5fd669690c4b80754c46f09d04273adf2ccbfb6563342677c52c5cde8a91808","assessment_fingerprint":"517b100d2e9006e313ab6d84d4f0f31593b77832f395383ba2227779470cd034","assessment_summary":{"status":"stale","file":"index/provision_link_adjudications.jsonl","total":11481,"expected":12455,"applied":0,"stale":11481,"unmatched":0,"unassessed":12455},"parent_id":"bco:10","children":[],"coverage":{"relationships":"indexed_records","recommendations":{"status":"incomplete","note":"Recommendation and study papers are not comprehensively indexed by provision."},"history":"partial"},"relationship_count":9,"relationships":[{"id":"bco:10-3--inquiry:inquiries/ga17_1989__ci02.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga17_1989__ci02.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Applicability of BCO 10-3 sermon and moderator-absence procedures to presbyteries","year":1989,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga17_1989__ci02.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga17_1989__ci02.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:10-3--inquiry:inquiries/ga17_1989__ci02.md:occ-e9dcb3066ee4","url":"https:/